    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Follow the Queen',
            subtitle: 'The Wild Card Stud Chaos',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Follow the Queen is one of the most unpredictable and chaotic variations of Seven Card Stud. While it follows the standard Stud structure, it introduces a roving wild card mechanic that can change mid-hand. The core rule is that Queens are wild, and the rank of the card dealt immediately after a Queen (the 'Trailer') also becomes wild. This creates massive hand rankings where Five-of-a-Kind is not just possible, but frequent, and the lead can shift dramatically with a single card deal.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "A popular home game variant from the mid-20th century, Follow the Queen was designed to inject high volatility into the otherwise methodical game of Seven Card Stud. It is a staple of 'Dealer's Choice' poker nights across North America.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '2 to 7 players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard Seven Card Stud deal: 2 down, 4 up, 1 down.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
    description: "Follow the Queen is one of the most unpredictable and chaotic variations of Seven Card Stud. While it follows the standard Stud structure, it introduces a roving wild card mechanic that can change mid-hand. The core rule is that Queens are wild, and the rank of the card dealt immediately after a Queen (the 'Trailer') also becomes wild. This creates massive hand rankings where Five-of-a-Kind is not just possible, but frequent, and the lead can shift dramatically with a single card deal.",
